WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.139
Hi everyone, thanks again for being a part of this class

2
00:00:04.139 --> 00:00:06.099
and I hope you got a lot out of it.

3
00:00:06.099 --> 00:00:07.940
What we covered today was different ways

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.619
to be able to create your layered materials,

5
00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:13.460
the old school way, the mega scans way,

6
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.900
as well as the new way to be able to do so

7
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.480
and how efficient that works.

8
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.179
We also covered MPCs,

9
00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:22.640
how to use material parameter collections,

10
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.780
how to get them set up in Sequencer

11
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.019
and how to just mainly get a good foundation for them

12
00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:29.559
and build them within your material

13
00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:33.250
to be able to do whatever you want.

14
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.009
We also talked about materials

15
00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:38.409
in the case of subsurface profiles,

16
00:00:38.409 --> 00:00:41.049
as well as subsurface materials in general

17
00:00:41.049 --> 00:00:45.469
and we also looked at the occlusion parallax occlusion

18
00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:47.409
and how to actually set that up

19
00:00:47.409 --> 00:00:50.240
and how that works in general also.

20
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.299
As well as looking at advanced subsurface materials

21
00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:56.759
when it came to creating such things as ice.

22
00:00:56.759 --> 00:00:59.359
Each one of these topics I hope you got a lot out of

23
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.039
and we hope to see you soon again in our classroom.

24
00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:02.880
Thanks again.
